request: Rename Todo.done to Todo.completed everywhere. --behaviour

governor turn 1: plan -> commands  (The only failure is in my own acceptance test. It wrongly claimed that list() hides completed todos by default, which is a behaviour change the rename never asked for. The transcript shows the default list includes completed items. I'm replacing that test with one that only checks the rename, and telling the owner to keep the current behaviour.)
round 1: owners commands=ok; oracle GREEN
governor turn 2: accept  (The oracle is green: tsc exits 0 and all 13 vitest tests pass. The Todo type now declares `completed: boolean` and has no `done` field. The saved todos.json uses `completed`. The acceptance test checks that add, complete and list use `completed` and that nothing has a `done` property. The CLI output is unchanged, as a rename should leave it. ListOptions.includeDone is the name of a list option, not a Todo field, so I kept it as it is.)

